## Section-A: Audit Policy

## l. Introduction

Audit policy  of bank sets a framework within which auditing activities are carried  out in the bank.  Audit policy  is enacted for regulating  all auditing activities  held at bank to achieve  greater effectiveness and efficiency  and to produce a credible assurance to all the stakeholders;  i.e.  management,  audit committee and the board.

 The objectives ofthe Audit Policy  are as follows:

- Ll To serve as a guiding reference  document for all auditing  function/activities ofthe  bank;
- 1.2 To prescribe a professional, structured and risk focused  standardized  audit methodology  for all auditing  functions,  products, and processes,  which is well regarded  by the regulators  and extemal agencies;
- 1.3 To develop a highly effective  audit function  that successfully combines the ability to detect all major control  weaknesses and minimize related control failures  and help manage the risks that  the bank faces  to support and guide  the Bank's businesses in achieving  their objectives;
- 1.4 To stipulate  the duties, responsibilities  and power  of the auditors,  senior  management,  audit committee and board with regards to audit function  in bank;
- 1.5 To lay down a structured organizational  audit system, and platform  for producing a credible assurance  to stakeholders;

Audit committee/board  shall review the audit policy annually or as deemed appropriate  since the revision  and amendment  in policy  is considered  as a continuous process.   Amendment/revision  to this policy may be approved  by the board on recommendation  of audit committee.  The amendment/ revision  shall be effective  only after the approval ofthe  Board.   Every effort  has been made to make this audit  policy  comprehensive  and consistent with the provisions of prevailing  bank and financial institution  act, company act, NRB directives  and other regulatory  requirements.   ln case of any contradiction  with them,  provisions  in this policy shall be superseded  by them.  ln all other  conditions, provisions ofthis policy  shall  prevail  to guide  the audit functions  in bank.  This  Audit  Policy replaces the existing Audit  Policy of the bank fiom the date of its approval.  All the acts carried  out under previous Audit Policy  is deemed to have been carried out under this policy.   Additionally,  any amendments  in the existing Rules/Regulations/directives  affecting  the provisions  of this audit policy shall have automatic effect ofamending  such provisions.

