Intemal audit department is formed  and designed  to generate reasonable  assurance that an effective system of intemal  control,  risk management,  compliance and corporate  govemance has been  designed and implemented in bank.   For the purpose  ofgenerating  reasonable  assurance as aforesaid,  the scope and responsibilities  of intemal  audit department  include but not limited to the following:

- 20.1. review all departmental functions  within  the Bank as appropriate to determine whether such functions  are efficiently  and effectively carried  out in accordance  with established  objectives, policies,  procedures,  practices  and standfids;
- 20.2. determine  the soundness, adequacy, effectiveness  and application  of financial and other management  systems and intemal  controls;
